review_comments:
Users may change the value of `Error.stackTraceLimit` at any time, the stored value could be outdated by the time it's read.
```suggestion
    }
    const userStackTraceLimit = Error.stackTraceLimit;
```

You should be able to hack your way around it in Node.js v16.0.0+ by making the `stackTraceLimit` not writable:
```js
Reflect.defineProperty(Error, 'stackTraceLimit', {
  writable: false,
  value: 0,
});
```
